# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in:  cp env.template .env && chmod 600 .env
# agent.sh loads .env from its own directory. Variables already exported in your shell win.
# Uncomment only the lines you fill in. Values are plain text on disk; the README's Keychain
# setup is the safer alternative.

# --- Image builds (./agent.sh xcode | tools) ---

# Password for the "admin" user inside the VMs. The build replaces the base image's default
# admin/admin login with this. Choose any strong password and keep it in your password manager;
# you need it to log in to a VM as admin.
# PKR_VAR_admin_password=

# Optional: SSH public key that job VMs accept for user "agent" (default ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub).
# Create one if you don't have it:  ssh-keygen -t ed25519
# Changing it takes effect after:   ./agent.sh tools
# PKR_VAR_ssh_pubkey_path=~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

# --- Jobs & sessions (./agent.sh run | session) ---

# Claude credentials, ONE of these. If both are set, only the OAuth token is passed to the VM.
#
# Option 1: subscription token (Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise). On your Mac run:
#   claude setup-token
# Sign in in the browser; it prints a token valid for one year (it isn't saved anywhere, so
# copy it now). Runs count against your plan's usage limits. Anyone with the token can use your
# plan, and it's exposed inside the VM; if it leaks, revoke it in your Claude account settings
# (claude.ai -> Settings, https://claude.ai/settings) or contact support, and generate a new one.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
#
# Option 2: API key (pay per token). Use a key dedicated to this purpose, with a spend limit;
# treat it as exposed to the VM.
#   Create the key:  Claude Console -> Settings -> API keys -> Create key
#                    https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
#   Spend limits:    Claude Console -> Settings -> Limits
#                    https://platform.claude.com/settings/limits
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# GitHub token, READ-ONLY. Its read-only permission is what actually prevents pushes.
# Create it at GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens ->
# Fine-grained tokens -> Generate new token
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# (manage/rotate existing ones under Fine-grained tokens:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens)
# Settings:
#   Repository access: only the repos the agent needs, including private Swift package deps.
#   Permissions:       Contents: Read-only (Metadata read is added automatically).
#                      Add Issues / Pull requests: Read-only only if your jobs read them.
#   Expiration:        short, and rotate it.
# GH_TOKEN=github_pat_...
